			"Message": "feat(Cocoon/Platform): Add unified module index for Platform exports\n\nThis commit introduces a comprehensive index file that centralizes and organizes all exports from Cocoon's Platform module, including OS, Environment, Process, TypeConverter, and Service. It provides a clean, single-point import for consumers, enabling easier integration with Wind's Effect-TS services and other parts of the Land ecosystem.\n\nThe index file re-exports all members from each submodule, grouped by module, and provides direct convenience exports for common operations. This follows the modular architecture established in previous commits and ensures that all platform functionality is accessible through type-safe, declarative imports. The extensive documentation included in the index clarifies module responsibilities, usage patterns, and connections to other elements (Mountain, Wind, etc.).\n\nThis unified export completes the Platform module's public API, streamlining development and setting the foundation for upcoming Vine gRPC integration by ensuring all necessary DTO conversion functions and platform abstractions are readily available.",
			"SHA": "534c2789fe82aeff9eccab4bbe24497381e9c6e8"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-01-31T03:00:30Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				524,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Cocoon/Platform): Add comprehensive DTO converter for Mountain IPC communication\n\nThis commit introduces the critical TypeScript-side data translation layer for the Cocoon extension host platform services. The `TypeConverter` module establishes bidirectional conversion between Cocoon's internal Platform types (`OSInfo`, `EnvironmentInfo`, `ProcessInfo`) and Mountain's DTO format, enabling structured IPC communication via Tauri commands and the planned Vine gRPC protocol.\n\nThe implementation provides conversion functions for all previously built Platform modules, including OS detection, environment variables, and process management. Each converter handles validation, sanitization, and serialization with security-conscious design (detecting sensitive environment variables, validating platform enums). The module exports placeholder Mountain DTO interfaces that will be updated to match exact Mountain backend definitions, establishing a clear protocol contract between Cocoon and Mountain.\n\nThis converter serves as the data adaptation layer between Cocoon's declarative Effect-TS service architecture and Mountain's native Rust backend, enabling Wind's services to consume platform functionality through type-safe DTOs. It completes the Cocoon platform abstraction by adding the IPC translation layer necessary for the Vine gRPC communication system.",
			"SHA": "63637c977722fff50342aa08e5540b74b1a1c40a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-01-31T02:59:25Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				523,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Cocoon/Platform): Unify platform modules into comprehensive Effect-TS service layer\n\nThis commit establishes the central integration layer for Cocoon's platform abstraction modules (`OS`, `Environment`, `Process`, `TypeConverter`) by introducing a comprehensive `PlatformService`. The service follows Land's declarative effects-based architecture, providing dependency injection, lifecycle management, and performance optimization for all platform operations within the TypeScript extension host sidecar.\n\nThe implementation creates an `IPlatformService` interface with corresponding `PlatformService` class that orchestrates platform operations with caching, health monitoring, and proper error handling. Key architectural features include: Effect-TS context and layer definitions (`PlatformServiceTag`, `PlatformServiceLayer`) for dependency injection; performance optimization through TTL-based caching; integrated DTO conversion functions that prepare data for synchronization with Mountain via the forthcoming Vine gRPC protocol; and complete service lifecycle management with initialization and disposal.\n\nThis service layer serves as the critical integration point between Cocoon's platform modules and Wind's Effect-TS services, enabling Wind components to consume platform functionality through declarative effects while maintaining the architectural separation between Mountain's native backend and Cocoon's extension host. It completes the platform abstraction layer begun in previous commits, establishing the foundation for platform-aware extension services and coordinated native operations across the Land ecosystem.",
			"SHA": "362c026ebebc5ab06e85fb880c14a81aeaccd15a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-01-31T02:57:21Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				522,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Cocoon/Platform): Introduce comprehensive child process management system\n\nThis commit establishes a foundational process management module for Cocoon's TypeScript extension host environment, completing the platform layer abstraction within the Land ecosystem's declarative effects-based architecture. It provides secure, declarative utilities for child process lifecycle management that will be critical for running VS Code extensions and language servers.\n\nThe implementation includes:\n- Core interfaces (`ProcessInfo`, `ProcessExitStatus`, `ProcessSpawnOptions`) following Cocoon's declarative DTO patterns\n- Security validation functions (`ValidateCommand`, `ValidateArgs`) with injection attack prevention\n- Effect-TS wrapped operations (`SpawnProcessEffect`, `ExecuteCommandEffect`) for integration into Cocoon's service layer\n- Process registry for tracking managed processes with automatic cleanup\n- Platform-specific signal handling with graceful termination strategies\n\nThis module serves as the TypeScript-side counterpart to Mountain's native process controls, establishing the process management abstraction that will be coordinated via future Vine gRPC synchronization. The security-focused design integrates with the existing PatchProcess security system by validating commands and arguments, creating a secure process execution environment for the extension host sidecar.",
			"SHA": "d8d10a34f54897d285122cee978e523f949dd039"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-01-31T02:54:04Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				521,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Cocoon/Platform): Establish comprehensive OS detection and platform information system\n\nThis commit introduces the foundational `OS.ts` module in Cocoon's platform layer, completing the TypeScript environment abstraction for OS-specific operations within the Land ecosystem. The module provides declarative, Effect-TS wrapped utilities for cross-platform development, directly supporting Cocoon's extension host services with robust platform detection and normalization.\n\nThe implementation includes comprehensive OS detection for Node.js and web environments (Windows, macOS, Linux), architecture identification, locale/language resolution with VSCODE_NLS_CONFIG compatibility, path normalization utilities, and Effect-TS wrapped functions for seamless integration into Cocoon's declarative service layer. Following VSCode patterns from the Microsoft/Dependency submodules, the module establishes the `OSInfo` DTO structure ready for IPC synchronization with Mountain's native backend via the planned Vine gRPC protocol.\n\nThis foundational platform detection supports upcoming integration with Mountain's native OS operations, enabling coordinated platform-specific behavior across Cocoon's extension host and Wind's Effect-TS services. The module's architecture provides the type-safe platform abstraction layer crucial for Land's declarative, effects-based cross-platform approach.",
			"SHA": "a3209d779c71d2162ee9ba4ec7c34c063d7b8d83"
		}
	],
	"TimeStamp": 1778420696020
